1. Explain about Tester’s Responsibility
A tester is responsible for performing Quality Control (QC) activities, mainly by executing test cases to find bugs and issues in a software product. Testers are part of the QC process, which comes under the broader QA process. 

The main responsibilities of a tester are:
(i)Understand and analyze the requirements.
(ii)Identify unclear requirements and clarify them with the concerned team.
(iii)Identify the types of testing required, such as functional, security, and performance testing.
(iv)Prepare test cases and test data.
(v)Set up and verify the test environment using smoke testing.
(vi)Execute test cases and mark them as Passed, Failed, Blocked, or Not Run.
(vii)Report defects and assign bug IDs.
(viii)Perform retesting after defects are fixed.
(ix)Track defects until they are closed.
(x)Prepare test execution reports, test metrics, and the test closure report.  

2. Explain about STLC Process
STLC - Software Testing Life Cycle. It is a systematic process followed by testers to perform testing activities throughout the testing life cycle.

The main phases of STLC are:
1.Requirement Analysis – The tester studies the requirements, identifies unclear points, asks questions, and determines the types of testing required. 
2.Test Planning – The testing scope, objectives, testing types, resources, tools, schedule, roles, responsibilities, risks, and testing criteria are defined. 
3.Test Case Development – Test cases, test data, and automation scripts, if required, are prepared based on the requirements. 
4.Test Environment Setup – The required hardware and software are identified, the test environment is set up, and smoke testing is performed to check its readiness. 
5.Test Execution – Test cases are executed and marked as Passed, Failed, Blocked, or Not Run. Defects are reported, retesting is performed after fixing, and defects are tracked until closure. 
6.Test Cycle Closure – The testing results are evaluated based on coverage, quality, cost, time, and business objectives. Test metrics and the Test Closure Report are prepared. 

STLC Flow:
Requirement Analysis -> Test Planning -> Test Case Development -> Test Environment Setup -> Test Execution -> Test Cycle Closure.
